  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Denmark&apos;s support to the partnership project between EHRC and DIHR 2025-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With this engagement Denmark will support the second phase of the partnership project between the Danish Institute for Human Rights (DIHR) and the Ethiopian Human Rights Commission (EHRC) supported through a DIHR-managed multi-donor basket fund. The project will support EHRC to fulfil its mandate to protect and promote human rights in conjunction with state and non-state actors as well as with regional and international bodies. The focus of this phase is consolidation and as such aims to gradually increase the EHRC&#x2019;s responsibility for the management of the project. Increased attention will be given to areas identified as needing further attention following the first phase of the DIHR-managed multi-donor basket fund support to EHRC (2020-2024) including human resources, standardization, monitoring and evaluation, safety and security and the EHRC expansion in the regions across the country. 

Furthermore, support will be given for the EHRC to develop and implement strategic plans; strengthen tools and procedures around early warming, rapid response and special investigations; engage in -and support national initiatives including transitional justice and national dialogue and to; establish and maintain a training center. These additional interventions will lead to a consolidation of the EHRC as an effective and independent NHRI in line with the UN Paris Principles. The EHRC will continue to address emerging issues such as human rights and business, climate change, digital rights, etc. as appropriate. The EHRC will continue to mainstream gender and disability as cross-cutting issues in all its activities as per its gender mainstreaming guidelines and inclusion strategy. 

This project directly contributes to Pillar 3 of the Danish Ethiopia Country Strategic Framework 2025 &#x2013; 2029: &#x2018;promote human rights, social cohesion, peace and stability&#x2019;. The project objective is: &#x2018;The Ethiopian Human Rights Commission fulfils its mandate to promote and protect human rights in conjunction with state and non-state actors as well as with regional and international bodies&#x2019;.</narrative>
  </description>
